### GCP authentication troubleshooting

Cloud Shell normally authenticates Terraform automatically. These steps are only needed if authentication fails, for example:

`oauth2/google: invalid token JSON from metadata: EOF`

Authenticate using your authorized deployment administrator:

```bash
gcloud auth login admin@x.com
gcloud config set account admin@x.com
```

Supply Terraform a temporary access token without printing it:

```bash
export GOOGLE_OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN="$(gcloud auth print-access-token \
  --account=admin@xc.com)"
```

Retry Terraform from the original deployment directory, keeping its existing state. Afterward, clear the token:

```bash
unset GOOGLE_OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN
```

The token expires; regenerate it if needed. Never share or commit it.
